      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Human handling is needed because proof is contributor-owned and the remaining merge choice is compatibility/security-boundary acceptance, not an automatable code repair.; Cleared: The diff tightens exec inline-eval detection and changes only TypeScript source/tests, with no dependency, workflow, secret, package, or supply-chain surface changes. (sha=19524888fca65b846bb2ee41f18e04e9f9172f3c)",
      "review_summary": "This PR expands shared exec inline-eval detection to recognize joined exact flags, equals-joined long flags, and selected short-option clusters, with regression coverage for strict allow-always persistence.\n\nPR surface: Source +182, Tests +100. Total +282 across 3 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. from source inspection, but not from a full live OpenClaw run. Current main only has exact and declared prefix matching while strict allow-always persistence depends on the shared inline-eval detector, so joined forms can miss the one-shot boundary.",
